  "body": "### Description\n\nWhen polling new events using the /sync endpoint, new events are not there instantly but with a delay of about 1.5 Minutes.\r\nHowever the messages can be seen instantly when using a Matrix Client like element.\r\nFurthermore the problem seems to be kinda solved when using long polling. Then only the first few requests will delay, but every following requests will get the new events instantly.\r\n\r\nThe problem is not there when using the /rooms/roomId/messages endpoint\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Write a message to a user using matrix\r\n- Poll the message using /sync\r\n- You will see a delay of about 30 seconds to 1.5 minutes\n\n### Homeserver\n\nPrivate homeserver (won't publish the url here)\n\n### Synapse Version\n\n{\"server_version\":\"1.73.0\",\"python_version\":\"3.9.2\"}\n\n### Installation Method\n\nI don't know\n\n### Database\n\nSQLiteV3.34.1 \n\n### Workers\n\nSingle process\n\n### Platform\n\nDebian on a VM with about 12 GB of RAM and 8 CPU Cores\n\n### Configuration\n\n_No response_\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\nDon't have any logs right now, can provide them later if needed\n```\n\n\n### Anything else that would be useful to know?\n\n_No response_",
